 *
 * Bespoke page (not the YAML-driven generic ProductPage), built to mirror the
 * sibling spokes src/pages/acoustic-strips.astro, src/pages/screed-isolation.astro,
 * src/pages/acoustic-underlay.astro and src/pages/sports-track-underlay.astro —
 * same class helpers, progressive-enhancement scroll-reveal motion, hand-rolled
 * breadcrumb and combined JSON-LD @graph (prefix `ht-`).
 *
 * ─── ROUTING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * This file serves /hammer-top. The content entry
 * src/content/products/hammer-top.yaml has been re-slugged from
 * `/horse-stable-mats/hammer-top` to `path: /hammer-top` and the matching branch
 * filtered out of getStaticPaths in src/pages/[...slug].astro — the same pattern
 * already used for acoustic-underlay, sports-track-underlay, screed-isolation,
 * acoustic-strips, zainfit, zainsquare, zainduo, zainactive-rolls and curb-stone
 * (and the /outdoor-pavers/dogbone + /hexagon re-slug). The YAML entry stays as
 * data (still a child of the `animal` hub); this file serves the URL. Internal
 * links that pointed at the old nested path were updated in
 * animal-agricultural-flooring.astro, shop.astro, blog/[slug].astro and
 * src/content/posts/best-flooring-horse-stables-uae-climate.md.
 *
 * ─── DECISIONS TAKEN / FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 "Data Integrity" + §6) ─────────
 *  - PARENT HUB: the build request's breadcrumb JSON-LD names the parent
 *    "Horse Stable Mats" at /horse-stable-mats on host rukanalzain.com. That
 *    route does not exist in this project — the real parent hub is the animal
 *    category hub /animal-agricultural-flooring (hammer-top.yaml `hub: animal`,
 *    and that hub already lists this page under `children`). Both the visible
 *    breadcrumb and the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD below use the real path with the
 *    label "Animal & Agricultural Flooring" — the same substitution already made
 *    on the acoustic siblings. NOTE: public/images/horse-stable-mats-hub/ and the
 *    `/horse-stable-mats/*` path prefix on horse-mats.yaml suggest a dedicated
 *    "Horse Stable Mats" sub-hub is planned. TODO: confirm the intended parent
 *    hub label / slug with the client; if the sub-hub ships, repoint crumb #2.
 *  - CANONICAL HOST: the request shows "rukanalzain.com/hammer-top"; the
 *    configured site is "ruknalzain.ae" (astro.config.mjs — note the
 *    spelling: ruk*n*alzain, not ruk*an*alzain). Canonical + all schema URLs are
 *    built from the configured site via BaseLayout `canonical={PATH}` (same
 *    choice as the siblings). TODO: confirm the production domain / spelling.
 *  - H1: the request gives two different H1 strings — "Zain Hammer Top —
 *    Textured Livestock & Farm Mats Dubai" (PAGE METADATA block) and "Zain
 *    Hammer Top — Heavy-Duty Stable & Farm Flooring Dubai" (Section 1 Hero).
 *    The single visible <h1> uses the Section 1 Hero string (the section that
 *    structures the page); the <title> tag uses the request's Title Tag verbatim.
 *  - DESIGN SYSTEM: the request describes React / Lucide-React icons / a generic
 *    Tailwind palette. This is a static Astro site (zero-JS). The page follows
 *    the live charcoal / industrial-grey design system with a single amber
 *    action accent and bordered "ghost" WhatsApp buttons; Lucide icons are
 *    inlined as raw SVG path data (no runtime). The FAQ accordion uses native
 *    <details>/<summary>.
 *  - TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS: hammer-top.yaml lists "Mat size" (mm) and
 *    "Thickness" (mm) as null "to collect". Every spec row rendered below is the
 *    descriptive text supplied in the page-build request, NOT numeric data from
 *    "Rukn_Al_Zain_SEO_Content_Brief V2.docx". The density figure
 *    (900–1100 kg/m³) is from the request, not a manufacturer certificate.
 *    Treat the whole table as PROVISIONAL and confirm against real product data
 *    / manufacturer certificates before go-live.
 *  - STRUCTURED DATA: a single combined @graph (BreadcrumbList + Product +
 *    FAQPage) is emitted inline. The request supplied BreadcrumbList + FAQPage;
 *    the FAQPage node is reproduced 1:1 from the on-page FAQ (identical to the
 *    request) and a Product node is added per CLAUDE.md §5. Organization JSON-LD
 *    is emitted sitewide by BaseLayout.
 *
 * ─── IMAGE ASSETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * public/images/horse-mats/ — intrinsic dimensions (all 1376×768) wired below
 * to prevent layout shift. public/ images use a plain <img> (astro:assets
 * <Image /> only optimises src/assets imports; there is no
